* Input-protection devices for the reverse-polarity sim. NOT vendor models: fitted stand-ins,
* kept with this study because nothing else uses them.
*
* SI2309CDS P-MOSFET, Level 1 (Vishay Si2309CDS datasheet, doc 68980 Rev. A):
*   VGS(th) -1 to -3 V (VTO = -1.5 here; lower |VTO| turns on more easily, the worst case for
*   capacitive turn-on during hot-plug). RDS(on) 0.345 ohm max at VGS = -10 V:
*   KP = 1 / (0.345 * (10 - 1.5)) = 0.341 A/V^2. Ciss 210 pF, Coss 28 pF, Crss 20 pF at
*   VDS = -30 V, fixed here: Cgd = 20p, Cgs = 190p, Cds = 8p. Body diode VSD 0.8 V typ at 0.75 A.
*   IDSS (1 uA max at -60 V) is not modeled; it is reported from the datasheet.
* Pins: D G S
.subckt SI2309CDS d g s
M1 d g s s PM_SI2309
Cgs g s 190p
Cgd g d 20p
Cds d s 8p
Dbody d s DBODY_SI2309
.ends SI2309CDS
.model PM_SI2309 PMOS(LEVEL=1 VTO=-1.5 KP=0.341 LAMBDA=0.01)
.model DBODY_SI2309 D(IS=1e-9 N=1.5 RS=0.1 BV=60 CJO=30p)
*
* SMAJ33CA bidirectional TVS as two series zeners (breakdown 36.7 V min per the SMAJ family).
.subckt SMAJ33CA a b
D1 a m DTVS
D2 b m DTVS
.ends SMAJ33CA
.model DTVS D(IS=1e-12 N=1 RS=0.3 BV=36.7 IBV=1m CJO=1n)
*
* BZT52C15 15 V zener (gate-source clamp).
.model DZ15 D(IS=1e-14 N=1 RS=5 BV=15 IBV=5m CJO=40p)
